# Showing L is standard: the terminal reduction

Aschbacher–Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*, combined manuscript
of 1 March 2004, §16.3, printed pp.1177–1182 / PDF pp.1194–1199.

The current development proves the terminal-to-standard implication under
16.3.1's explicit conjugate-component exclusion, the normalizer consequence
16.3.3, and the construction of a contrary involution in T_C under the earlier
relative normality conclusion 16.2.4. E1 alone supplies even order of L. The
shared contrary setup and the literal dihedral/semidihedral conclusion of
16.3.8 are available for independent downstream arguments.

Theorem 16.3.7 remains open: the exclusion in 16.3.1, the transfer and shape
arguments 16.3.4–8, the enlargement reductions 16.3.9–11, and the Thompson
calculation 16.3.12 are still required. Lemma 16.3.13(3), used by §16.4, also
remains to be assembled. The general Sylow centralizer obstruction supplies
the last inference on p.1182 once the actual Thompson data are proved.
-/
